                <pb facs="0319" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11320: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-12T16:00:00+08:00">December 12, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 12—3:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>134. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“December 12, 3 p.m. Chiang Kai-shek, who is now in Kuling, has offered a
                            reward of 50,000 dollars for the capture of Chu, Mao, Peng and Hwang,
                            bandit leaders in Kiangsi.</p>
                        <p>Chiang Kai-shek has ordered the dismissal, arrest and trial of General
                            Teng, now of the new 13th Division, for failure to carry out ordinance
                            to advance against communist army recently in occupation of Kian.</p>
                        <p>U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Guam</hi> was in action yesterday just
                            below and above Chenglingki in answer to attacks from ashore by trench
                            mortars and rifle fire. Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
